From 30e6b8cb605934876837edd5654a948b08937edd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:57:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 10/14] test(v2): version 7 helpers, bridge signers and shared
 signing vectors

test_framework/v7tx.py builds version 7 transactions and computes the V2
signing message of a spend invocation (lotus::v2::SigningMessage), with the
legacy coin wire and the legacy bridge selector leaf. It signs P2PKH bridge
inputs (BIP340 over the message) and P2SH bridge inputs (a legacy ECDSA
signature plus hashtype 0x41/0xC1/0xC3 over the message of the mode the
hashtype selects), and adds MiniWalletV7: V2 OP_TRUE coins funded by
bridging a legacy MiniWallet's P2SH(OP_TRUE) coins.

src/test/data/v2_legacy_bridge.json holds nine signing-message vectors
(P2PKH and 2-of-2 P2SH bridge inputs in modes 0-2, with height and
relative locks, and a bridge input beside a V2 coin). The C++ test
v2_legacy_bridge_vector_tests/signing_message_vectors rebuilds and checks
them (LOTUS_V2_BRIDGE_VECTORS_OUT regenerates the file); the framework
unit test TestFrameworkV7Tx checks the Python implementation against the
same file, a legacy round trip with SHA256d naming, and BIP340 signing.

Fix the framework's V2 output decoder, which dropped path indices, so a
decoded output had empty paths and a wrong wire.

lotus_v2_loopback_tps_stress uses the promoted V2 output helper.

Rebase onto coordinator 276 (81e8ef1774): the framework's MiniWallet is a
V2 wallet on this stack, so v7tx adds LegacyMiniWallet, the P2SH(OP_TRUE)
legacy MiniWallet (legacy coinbases, scantxoutset) that fund_from and the
bridge test use. test_runner lists both v7tx and the coordinator's worker
module.

Tier: V2
